# SYNTHETIC TRAINING DATA: not a real financial institution or a product-native export.
# FIRST-PASS EXTRACT: related ACCOUNT daily-close workflow, BALANCE_QUERY_API and ACCTDB only.
# range=2026-10-08..2026-10-14; daily extraction window=[18:00,23:00); timezone=Asia/Seoul (+09:00).
# Filtered records are normalized to key=value fields; irrelevant fields are omitted, not zero-filled.
# Investigation comparison remains 2026-10-13 versus 2026-10-12 and 2026-10-14, [19:30,21:50).
# Identifiers are synthetic stable join keys. Samples are not a full event or transaction trace.
# Human-readable normalized Db2-style monitoring events, NOT raw db2diag.log format.
# Source scenario: database metrics, connection-pool telemetry, activity samples and retained lock-monitor events.
# DB_HEALTH_SAMPLE and BUFFERPOOL_IO_SAMPLE: database scope. CONNECTION_POOL_SAMPLE: BALANCE_QUERY_API cluster scope.
# Window summaries carry explicit [window_start,window_end); the event timestamp is near the window end.
# Activity elapsed_sec is cumulative for that SQL activity. Missing SQL plans/statistics remain unavailable.
# LOCK_WAIT_SAMPLE shows observed waiter/holder at one moment; it does not establish why the batch SQL was slow.
# api_errors_5m in CSV = api_http_4xx_5m + api_http_5xx_5m; api_timeouts_5m is a subset of HTTP 5xx.
# CSV app metrics aggregate two API instances; DB metrics are database-wide. pct=0..100, ms=milliseconds, mb=MiB.
# CSV API percentiles/mean describe requests across the two instances in each non-overlapping five-minute window.
# Supplemental extract: one observed BALANCE_QUERY_API connection per minute in [19:00,22:00) on each date.
# SESSION_ACTIVITY_SAMPLE fields describe that connection/activity only; they are not totals, maxima, or a complete request trace.
# window_start joins each sample to its containing five-minute metrics window. Do not add session observations to CSV counters.
# app_handle is a synthetic stable connection key; uow_id/activity_id distinguish observed work on a reused connection.
# Only active samples include SQL activity fields. IDLE records omit fields that are not applicable.
# LOCK_WAIT indicates a sampled state, not a new lock-timeout event or proof of why the batch SQL was slow.
